## Cursor MCP servers (required)

This machine already has the live ProTech servers in Cursor `mcp.json` (`C:\Users\Admin\.cursor\mcp.json`). **Use those servers.** Do not invent a second WordPress or cPanel connection, and do not use Hostinger WP tools for this site.

| Job | `mcp.json` key | Cursor namespace | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| WordPress content (pages, posts, CPTs, media, users, WPML) | `wordpress-mcp` | `user-wordpress-mcp` | Application Password in `mcp.json` / `credential` |
| Hosting (files, domains, email, SSL, cron, DB, PHP) | `cpanel` | `user-cpanel` | cPanel API token in `mcp.json` / `credential` |

Site plugin: **WordPress MCP** (`wordpress-mcp-trunk`, Automattic, v0.2.5) — endpoint `/wp-json/wp/v2/wpmcp`. The local proxy is `@automattic/mcp-wordpress-remote`. `WP_API_URL` is the site root (`https://protech.lbp-support.com/`), not the MCP Adapter path.

```json
"wordpress-mcp": {
  "command": "npx",
  "args": [ "-y", "@automattic/mcp-wordpress-remote@latest" ],
  "env": {
    "WP_API_URL": "https://protech.lbp-support.com/",
    "WP_API_USERNAME": "ezz",
    "WP_API_PASSWORD": "(Application Password — credential / mcp.json only)",
    "OAUTH_ENABLED": "false"
  }
},
"cpanel": {
  "command": "node",
  "args": ["D:\\MCP\\cPanel-MCP-Server\\build\\index.js"],
  "env": {
    "CPANEL_USERNAME": "lbpsupport",
    "CPANEL_API_TOKEN": "(see credential / mcp.json)",
    "CPANEL_SERVER_URL": "https://cpanel.lbp-support.com:2083"
  }
}
```

Do not paste the Application Password or cPanel token into this file, chat, WPCode, or git.

## WordPress MCP (required)

Operate the site through **`user-wordpress-mcp`**. Pass `wpml_language` (`en` or `ar`) on tools that support it.

### Every session

1. Discover tools: `GetDynamicTools` namespace `user-wordpress-mcp` (or pattern `wordpress|wp_|wpmcp`).
2. Read the schema of the tool you will call before calling it.
3. Prefer MCP over REST-in-the-browser, wp-admin clicking, or invented local files.
4. If `user-wordpress-mcp` is missing, unauthorized, or has no content tools: call `mcp_auth` once. If it still fails, **stop and tell the user to reload the `wordpress-mcp` server in Cursor**. Do not improvise a parallel workflow.

Typical capabilities (always use the live schema):

- List/get/create/update posts, pages, and custom post types
- Media, menus, users, comments, categories, tags
- Site info, plugins, and settings (read before write)
- WPML language on most content tools (`wpml_language`: `en` / `ar`)

### Safer writes

- Read the current item first. Patch only what you need.
- After content updates, check the WPML translation of the same item.
- Do not activate/deactivate plugins, change permalinks, or edit WPML language settings unless the user asked.
- Do not store Application Passwords or admin passwords in the repo.

