## Server access — cPanel, SSH, WP-CLI

Use these when WordPress MCP is not enough. Read `credential` for URLs, usernames, tokens, and the SSH host alias. Do not paste secrets here or in chat.

### When to use which

| Need | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Pages, posts, CPTs, menus, media, users, comments | WordPress MCP |
| Hosting: files, domains, email, SSL, cron, databases, PHP, caches at the account level | **cPanel MCP** (`user-cpanel`) |
| Shell, SFTP, one-off server commands, WP-CLI | **SSH** (`ssh lbpsupport`) |
| Plugin/theme/core inspect, search-replace, cache flush, language packs, bulk WP ops | **WP-CLI** over SSH |

Prefer the least-destructive layer. Do not SSH-edit Divi theme files or dump custom PHP into the docroot when WPCode can hold it.

### cPanel

- Panel: `https://cpanel.lbp-support.com:2083`
- Account user: `lbpsupport` (password + API token in `credential`)
- Cursor MCP: `mcp.json` key `cpanel` → namespace `user-cpanel`. Discover tools (`GetDynamicTools` namespace `user-cpanel`, or pattern `cpanel|ssh|file|cron|php`) and read the schema before calling.
- MCP env is already in Cursor `mcp.json` (`CPANEL_SERVER_URL=https://cpanel.lbp-support.com:2083`, token named `Cursor-MCP`). If MCP 404s on the public site URL, the server URL is wrong — use the `:2083` host, not `protech.lbp-support.com/cpanel`.
- Site home: `/home/lbpsupport`
- ProTech docroot: `/home/lbpsupport/protech.lbp-support.com`
- After file/CSS/JS/layout changes, purge LiteSpeed (cPanel LiteSpeed cache and/or WP LiteSpeed). Also clear Divi static CSS when the front still looks stale.

### SSH

- Host alias (local `~/.ssh/config`): `ssh lbpsupport` — user `lbpsupport`, host `65.108.37.198`, port `3040`, key `~/.ssh/protech_lbpsupport`
- Optional alias `ssh protech` starts in the ProTech docroot
- Shell is enabled (bash). If you see `Shell access is not enabled`, stop and tell the user to enable Jail Shell / bash in **WHM → Manage Shell Access** for `lbpsupport`
- SFTP works on the same host/port/key even if shell is off
- Public key is in `/home/lbpsupport/.ssh/authorized_keys` (comment `protech-lbpsupport`)

```bash
ssh lbpsupport
# or a one-liner:
ssh lbpsupport 'cd ~/protech.lbp-support.com && wp plugin list'
```

### WP-CLI

Already installed on the server (WP Toolkit): `/usr/local/bin/wp` — version 2.12.0.

Project config: `/home/lbpsupport/protech.lbp-support.com/wp-cli.yml` (`path` + `url`). From the docroot you do not need `--path`.

```bash
ssh lbpsupport
cd ~/protech.lbp-support.com
wp --version
wp core version
wp plugin list
wp litespeed-purge all
```

Do not drop a web-accessible `wp-cli.phar` in the docroot. Do not run destructive WP-CLI (`plugin delete`, `db reset`, `search-replace` on production URLs) unless the user asked.

