## LiteSpeed Cache — purge after every change

Plugin **LiteSpeed Cache** (`litespeed-cache`) is installed and **active**. The server also runs LiteSpeed. Cached HTML/CSS/JS will hide new work until you purge.

**After every successful change** (Divi content, WPCode snippet, WPML, plugin/setting, file, CSS/JS), purge before you verify the front. A change that is only in the database or admin is unfinished if the public EN/AR pages still show the old cache.

```bash
ssh lbpsupport 'cd ~/protech.lbp-support.com && wp litespeed-purge all'
```

- `wp litespeed-purge all` is the required purge (plugin page cache + related LSCache).
- `wp cache flush` is WordPress object cache only. Use it as extra if needed, **not** instead of `litespeed-purge`.
- After visual/Divi changes, also clear **Divi static CSS**, then purge LiteSpeed.
- Then check **English and `/ar/`**. Do not treat an admin preview or a single cached screenshot as done.
- Do not deactivate or reconfigure LiteSpeed Cache unless the user asked.

---

## Divi — do not touch the theme

Divi stores layouts in the **database** (page/post content + Theme Builder). That is the only Divi surface you may change.

**Never:**

- Edit files under `wp-content/themes/Divi/`
- Create or edit a child theme unless the user explicitly orders it (default is **no**)
- Use Appearance → Theme File Editor
- Override Divi templates (`header.php`, `footer.php`, `functions.php`, module PHP)
- Change Divi core / Elegant Themes plugin files

**Allowed Divi work (via MCP / wp-admin, not files):**

- Page and CPT content built with Divi Builder
- Theme Builder layouts (header / footer / body) **and their WPML translations**
- Divi Library layouts / global modules — update the item and every language copy
- Module settings, design, and copy inside the builder

Divi extras on this site (do not patch their plugin files): Divi Builder API (`divi/v1`), DiviFlash (`difl/v5`), Divi menu/popup settings. Customize with WPCode hooks/CSS, or their own UI.

After visual changes: clear **Divi static CSS**, then **purge LiteSpeed Cache** (`wp litespeed-purge all`), then check EN + AR.

---

## Custom code = WPCode only

Plugin: **WPCode – Insert Headers and Footers + Custom Code Snippets – WordPress Code Manager**.

Use Code Snippets (or Headers & Footers for site-wide scripts). One concern per snippet. Name snippets so the next agent can find them.

| Need | WPCode type | Insertion |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PHP hooks, filters, shortcodes, REST tweaks | PHP Snippet | Auto Insert → Run Everywhere or Front-end only |
| Layout/visual CSS | CSS Snippet | Auto Insert → Site Wide Header |
| Behavior in the browser | JavaScript Snippet | Auto Insert → Site Wide Footer (unless it must be in `head`) |
| Markup / pixels / third-party tags | HTML Snippet | Header or Footer as the vendor requires |
| Analytics / GTM / chat widgets | Headers & Footers or HTML | Header or Footer |

**Snippet conventions**

- Title: `ProTech — {area} — {what}` e.g. `ProTech — Header — hide WPML banner`
- Code type must match the content (do not paste CSS into a PHP snippet)
- Prefer Auto Insert + location over editing Divi Integration
- Use WPCode conditionals (page, post type, logged-in) instead of huge `if` trees when possible
- For language-specific CSS/JS, gate on WPML (`ICL_LANGUAGE_CODE` in PHP, `html[lang]`, or `body.rtl` / `/ar/` in CSS). Still keep **one** snippet that covers both languages when the rule is shared
- Enable Safe Mode / keep a way to disable a broken snippet
- Never put secrets in snippets

Do **not** add a site-specific custom plugin, mu-plugin, or child-theme file for work that WPCode can hold.

---

## WPML — both languages, always

Confirmed on the live site:

| Language | Code | URL | Direction |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| English (default) | `en` | `https://protech.lbp-support.com/` | LTR |
| Arabic | `ar` | `https://protech.lbp-support.com/ar/` | RTL |

Do not assume these stay the only languages. At the start of a task, list languages via WordPress MCP or WPML. If a new language appears, include it.

### Content pairing (pages, as of last check)

English and Arabic pages are **separate posts** linked by WPML. Edit both (or translate via WPML), never only EN.

| English | EN ID | Arabic | AR ID |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Home | 17 | الرئيسية | 1866 |
| About | 19 | من نحن | 1861 |
| Our Services | 21 | الخدمات | 1869 |
| Products | 23 | المنتجات | 1868 |
| Blogs | 25 | المقالات | 1862 |
| Partners | 27 | الشركاء | 1867 |
| Careers | 29 | الوظائف | 1863 |
| Contact Us | 31 | تواصل معنا | 1865 |

IDs can change. Resolve the translation with WPML/MCP before editing.

Custom post types that also need EN + AR:

- `project` — Products (`/product/...`)
- `career` — Careers
- `partner` — Partners
- `post` — Blog articles

### WPML workflow

1. Find the item in the default language (English).
2. Find the translation (Arabic `+` / pencil in WPML, or MCP/REST `lang=ar`).
3. Apply the same **functional** change on both. Translate strings; do not leave English on `/ar/` or Arabic on `/`.
4. Theme Builder, global modules, menus, widgets, and CF7 forms are translatable too. A header change that only exists in EN is unfinished.
5. String Translation / WPML → Translation Dashboard for theme strings, admin texts, and Divi global variables when they are not in page content.
6. RTL: Arabic must look correct (alignment, icons, sliders, absolute positions). Shared CSS must not break LTR. Prefer logical properties (`margin-inline-start`) or `html[lang="ar"]` / `.rtl` overrides.
7. Menus: update **both** language menus and the language switcher labels/URLs.
8. Do not create a new EN page/CPT without creating and linking the AR translation (and the reverse).

WPML docs for Divi: [Translate Divi with WPML](https://wpml.org/documentation/theme-compatibility/divi-builder/).

---

## Where each change goes

| Change | Place | Not here |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Page/section copy, modules, spacing, images in a layout | Divi Builder on that page **and** its AR/EN twin | Theme files, WPCode (unless CSS/JS is required) |
| Global header / footer / body template | Divi Theme Builder + WPML translation of that layout | `header.php` / `footer.php` |
| Custom PHP | WPCode PHP snippet | `functions.php`, new plugin, mu-plugin |
| Custom CSS | WPCode CSS snippet | Divi theme stylesheet, child theme |
| Custom JS | WPCode JS snippet | Divi scripts, theme `js/` |
| Tracking / head-foot tags | WPCode Headers & Footers | Theme Integration tab (avoid unless user insists) |
| New landing page | WP page + Divi + WPML translation | PHP template |
| Products / partners / careers | CPT `project` / `partner` / `career` + translation | Hardcoded Divi modules only, unless that is already the pattern |
| Forms | Contact Form 7 + WPML | New form plugin |
| Redirects / cache | LiteSpeed / cPanel / WP-CLI `wp cache flush` | Random PHP redirects unless requested |
| Server files, cron, SSL, email, databases | cPanel MCP or SSH | Invented local files, Hostinger WP tools |
| Plugin/theme inspect, bulk WP ops, search-replace | WP-CLI over SSH | Theme file edits, custom plugins |

